{"subjectId":"python","id":"strings","title":"Strings","group":"Getting Started","order":3,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>str</code> is an immutable sequence of Unicode characters — indexing, slicing and methods all return <em>new</em> strings.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-cut\"></i>Indexing &amp; slicing</h3>\n<p><code>s[start:stop:step]</code> — <code>start</code> is included, <code>stop</code> is excluded, negative indices count from the end.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = \"interview\"\nprint(s[0], s[-1], len(s))      # i w 9\nprint(s[0:5], s[5:], s[-4:])    # inter view view\nprint(s[::-1], s[::2])          # weivretni itriw</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-lock\"></i>Immutability</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = \"cat\"\ntry:\n    s[0] = \"b\"\nexcept TypeError as e:\n    print(\"TypeError:\", e)       # TypeError: 'str' object does not support item assignment\ns = \"b\" + s[1:]                  # build a new string instead\nprint(s)                         # bat</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Performance</div><p>Building a string with <code>+=</code> in a loop can be O(n²). Collect pieces in a list and call <code>''.join(parts)</code> once — O(n).</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list\"></i>Essential methods</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Does</th><th>Example → result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>split(sep)</code> / <code>join(it)</code></td><td>String ↔ list</td><td><code>'a,b'.split(',')</code> → <code>['a', 'b']</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>strip()</code> / <code>lstrip()</code> / <code>rstrip()</code></td><td>Trim whitespace (or given chars)</td><td><code>' hi '.strip()</code> → <code>'hi'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>lower()</code> / <code>upper()</code> / <code>title()</code></td><td>Change case</td><td><code>'Py'.lower()</code> → <code>'py'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>find(x)</code> / <code>index(x)</code></td><td>Position or −1 / raises</td><td><code>'abc'.find('z')</code> → <code>-1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>replace(a, b)</code></td><td>Replace all occurrences</td><td><code>'aa'.replace('a','b')</code> → <code>'bb'</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>startswith</code> / <code>endswith</code></td><td>Prefix / suffix test</td><td><code>'file.py'.endswith('.py')</code> → <code>True</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>isdigit</code> / <code>isalpha</code> / <code>isalnum</code></td><td>Character classes</td><td><code>'123'.isdigit()</code> → <code>True</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>count(x)</code></td><td>Non-overlapping occurrences</td><td><code>'banana'.count('a')</code> → <code>3</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>words = \"  the quick  brown fox \".split()   # split() with no args handles runs of spaces\nprint(words)                                 # ['the', 'quick', 'brown', 'fox']\nprint(\"-\".join(words))                       # the-quick-brown-fox\nprint(\" \".join(w.capitalize() for w in words))   # The Quick Brown Fox</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-braces\"></i>f-strings &amp; formatting</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>name, score, ratio = \"Asha\", 93, 0.8567\nprint(f\"{name} scored {score}\")          # Asha scored 93\nprint(f\"{ratio:.2%} | {score:05d}\")      # 85.67% | 00093\nprint(f\"{name!r:&gt;8}|{score:&lt;5}|\")        #   'Asha'|93   |\nprint(f\"{score=}\")                       # score=93\nprint(f\"{1_000_000:,}\")                  # 1,000,000</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-language\"></i>Characters, Unicode &amp; bytes</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>print(ord(\"A\"), chr(97))                 # 65 a\nprint(len(\"naïve\"), len(\"naïve\".encode(\"utf-8\")))   # 5 6\nprint(\"é\".encode(), b\"\\xc3\\xa9\".decode())          # b'\\xc3\\xa9' é</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-letter-case\"></i><code>str</code></h3><p>Text — a sequence of Unicode code points.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-binary\"></i><code>bytes</code></h3><p>Raw 8-bit data — files, network, hashing. Convert with <code>encode()</code> / <code>decode()</code>.</p></div></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-star\"></i>Interview favourites</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def is_palindrome(s: str) -&gt; bool:\n    cleaned = [c.lower() for c in s if c.isalnum()]\n    return cleaned == cleaned[::-1]\n\ndef is_anagram(a: str, b: str) -&gt; bool:\n    from collections import Counter\n    return Counter(a) == Counter(b)\n\nprint(is_palindrome(\"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\"))   # True\nprint(is_anagram(\"listen\", \"silent\"))                    # True</code></pre></figure></section>"}